from lv import L
L("- Restate: cut a repeat or bare label of the last line, intensified or not, and any phrase marking speech as on record, honest, clear or said first; stammers stay.")
L("- Lulls: raise card interests and wants.",
  "- Work words, narration too: only for work underway, raised by others, due or dodged; feelings, memories, promises, decisions show as acts or choices.",
  "- Demands: press once; refused or sidestepped, act or trade, else drop it; move on; pet phrases rest four replies.",
  "- Demands: press once; refused or sidestepped, act or trade, else drop it and move on; pet phrases rest four replies.",
  "- Demands: press once, then, refused or sidestepped, act or trade, else drop it and move on; pet phrases rest four replies.",
  "- Demands: press once; refused or sidestepped, act or trade, else drop it and let the scene move on, pet phrases resting four replies.")
L("Native reasoning: one pass, a terse bullet per plan line, under 150 words, Tally aside; no drafts, rereads, audits or second passes, then write.",
  "Native reasoning: one terse bullet per plan line in a single pass, under 150 words besides Tally; no drafts, rereads, audits or second passes, then write.",
  "Native reasoning: one pass of a terse bullet per plan line, under 150 words besides Tally; no drafts, rereads, audits or second passes, then write.")
L("- Echo: answer {{user}}'s line by an act or own words, never by repeating it, single words too.",
  "- Bodies: if the card or first message describes a body, parts a plain human lacks, tails and wings included, appear only if named there, whatever the species.",
  "- Bodies: on a body the card or first message describes, parts a plain human lacks, tails and wings too, appear only if named there, any species; unnamed ones go unmentioned, hidden or absent alike.",
  "- Bodies: if the card or first message describes a body, parts a plain human lacks, tails and wings too, appear only if named there, any species, and unnamed ones go unmentioned, hidden or absent alike.")
L("- Joins: past one a reply, a sentence under five words joins a neighbour, a lone-sentence paragraph the one before if the same voice carries on; stalls and cut-offs, one-word answers stay.",
  "- Joins: past one a reply, a sentence under five words joins a neighbour, a lone-sentence paragraph the one before if the same voice carries on; stammers, stalls, cut-offs and one-word answers stay.")
L("Kept: names, colours, values, filled gaps as first set; counts, ages, images, paragraph layouts return only when the story changes them.",
  "Reactions: answer what was said or done, claims and stakes, by stance or act; dodge only as the card does.",
  "- Flow: narration sentences have their own subject and verb, five words or more; one person's small acts in a row share a sentence, two at most.")
